  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-the-image-data has special \"load synchronously\" behavior for `src`\n\nI think this generally makes sense, because `srcset` / `picture` might point to multiple images, and so if you triggered a bunch of appends to a `picture` element you'd end up triggering tons of loads if you don't coalesce them at the microtask level.\n\nI'm not sure the same reasoning applies to `srcset` tho. Furthermore, maybe we should allow pulling from the \"available image cache\" unconditionally, as that doesn't trigger image loads?\n\nThe context here is some pages depend on bugs in Chrome's image loading and flicker in Safari and Firefox, but it might be sensible to allow them to behave the same as they would behave with `src`. See https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2040530#c9 for some site / commentary / test-cases.\n\ncc @tnikkel @annevk @zcorpan @EdgarChen ",
